Interesting: after auto resume at t=300, the top still shows "自动暂停" but the speed is 23.7 and the timer advanced 4:36. The top label didn't update because data_tick auto-resumes by calling `toast("自动继续")` but does not rebuild the ride page, so the top label (built when paused) remains "自动暂停" while R.paused=false. The hero color stays gray? It shows dark "23.7" because ride_refresh sets hero color based on R.paused, but the top is stale. Need to update the pause top label when auto resume happens while on ride page. Simplest: in data_tick after ride_advance_1s, if screen RIDE and the pause state changed, rebuild. But rebuilding every tick when state changes is okay (only on change). Track `was_paused` before ride_advance, compare after; if changed and screen==RIDE → rebuild (not just refresh). Similarly if auto pause triggers while on ride page, the top won't update (only toast). The auto pause screenshot used freeze from initial state, so built paused. But runtime needs update.

Implement in data_tick:
```c
bool was_paused = R.paused;
ride_advance_1s();
if (s_screen == SCR_RIDE) {
  if (R.paused != was_paused) rebuild();
  else ride_refresh();
}
```
But rebuild from within data_tick is okay. Need to avoid rebuilding every tick. Do it.

Also if auto pause triggers while on nav/dial, no top to update.

Add.

